{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE MISSING PASS-LEVEL CELL IS WRITTEN — Gerrit 1341\n\n`test_outbound_epic_parent_reaches_dc_THROUGH_A_RECONCILE_PASS`: attaches the parent LOCALLY via `rebar.edit_ticket(child_local, parent=epic_local)`, runs a real `_WRITING_MODE` pass, and reads the child's Epic Link back over **raw REST** — never through the transport that performed the write, so a writer that returns cleanly without persisting cannot pass itself.\n\n**It asserts the emit-gate precondition rather than assuming it.** The local parent's `ticket_type` must be `epic`, because bug 8b25's hierarchy guard omits the parent field entirely unless it is. Without that guard, a seeded epic that imported as some other type would make the pass plan nothing, and the cell would go red as if the apply side had failed — unattributable, and exactly the SETUP-vs-defect confusion this module's split exists to prevent.\n\nThis is the cell AC1 actually asked for: it exercises the emit gate and the apply gate TOGETHER, which is the intersection the ticket is about. The pre-existing cell only ever proved the apply half.\n\nNot yet run — round-2 (30870845838) predates it. It rides the next harness run."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785810480538303001,"uuid":"57bf6e14-a48a-4b00-8dfa-dc92a556d9e6"}